{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" is a domain plugin that owns a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState"},{"type":"text","text":" slice, fetches a JSON wire format via a provider-agnostic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsService"},{"type":"text","text":", and answers reads against state. Bucketing is pure FNV-1a so reads are synchronous and offline-capable."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Three flag types from one wire format:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"boolean","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — on\/off with rollout percentage (0–100).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"variant","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — string-typed weighted variants for A\/B tests.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"value","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — typed remote-tunable scalar (","type":"text"},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For end-to-end wiring, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Library target","anchor":"Library-target","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Product: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxFeatureFlags"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Wire format","level":2,"anchor":"Wire-format"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["{","  \"version\": 1,","  \"flags\": {","    \"new_onboarding\": { \"type\": \"boolean\", \"rollout\": 25 },","    \"checkout_layout\": {","      \"type\": \"variant\",","      \"variants\": [","        { \"value\": \"control\", \"weight\": 50 },","        { \"value\": \"treatment\", \"weight\": 50 }","      ]","    },","    \"max_free_uploads\": { \"type\": \"value\", \"value\": 5 }","  }","}"],"syntax":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin rejects unknown "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" values and falls back to the last-known-good cache. Defaults always live in Swift at the call site — this keeps them type-checked and forces “what if missing?” thinking."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Bucketing and identity","anchor":"Bucketing-and-identity"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bucket = FNV1a(bucketingID + \":\" + flagKey) % 100"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Stable per ","type":"text"},{"code":"(bucketingID, flagKey)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pair forever.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Same input always produces the same bucket.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Per-flag."}]},{"text":" A user isn’t always in the “early” group across different flags.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identity resolution."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" When a ","type":"text"},{"code":"userIDKeyPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is configured ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the current user ID is non-nil, that is used. Otherwise the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"device ID","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is used (the plugin’s required "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceIDKeyPath"},{"type":"text","text":"). Anonymous users get a stable per-install identity; logged-in users get stable cross-device assignment. A user’s variant "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"can"}]},{"type":"text","text":" shift once at login — acceptable for nearly all real use cases."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"FNV-1a was chosen because it’s simple, dependency-free, and matches GrowthBook’s algorithm so apps migrating from GrowthBook get compatible buckets.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"The device ID must be stable across reinstall","anchor":"The-device-ID-must-be-stable-across-reinstall"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bucketing is only stable if the fallback identity is. The plugin takes a non-optional "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceIDKeyPath: KeyPath<State, String>"},{"type":"text","text":" into your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"app","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" owns the identity and the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" value can drive analytics ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.deviceID, …)"},{"type":"text","text":") — one identity, so A\/B exposure correlates with the user analytics reports against."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mint it once at launch with the shared core helper, backed by the Keychain so it survives reinstall, and seed it into the slice via "},{"code":"hydrated(from:deviceID:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ In Store.configured()","let deviceID = KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.app\").deviceIdentity()","","let plugin = FeatureFlagsPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.featureFlags, action: AppAction.featureFlags, extractAction: { … },","    service: service,","    deviceIDKeyPath: \\.deviceID,          \/\/ app-owned, Keychain-backed","    userIDKeyPath: \\.auth.currentUserID,  \/\/ optional; authed identity wins when set","    keyValueStore: kv",")","","let initial = AppState(","    featureFlags: .hydrated(from: kv, deviceID: deviceID),","    deviceID: deviceID",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-backed identity regenerates on reinstall (QA ad-hoc builds, test installs), which silently re-buckets users and breaks A\/B assignment — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" for the identity. The flags "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"config cache"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" can still live in a lighter store.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Evaluation order","anchor":"Evaluation-order","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For each read, in priority:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Local override present?","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Return it.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Flag in remote config?"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Evaluate (rollout \/ variant assignment \/ value lookup).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Otherwise"}]},{"type":"text","text":" return the Swift-side default."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"Persistence","anchor":"Persistence","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Device ID"}]},{"text":" is app-owned and minted once via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore.deviceIdentity()"},{"text":" (Keychain-backed). Seeded into the slice at ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState.hydrated(from:deviceID:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and kept in sync from ","type":"text"},{"code":"deviceIDKeyPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The plugin no longer mints its own bucketing identity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Last-known config","type":"text"}]},{"text":" persisted after every successful refresh. Hydrates as fallback before first network success.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Local overrides"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" persisted by default. Restart = clean state."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"exposedKeys","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" persisted. New session = fresh exposure events."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Governance-no-forever-flags","text":"Governance: no forever flags","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Owner and expiry are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"required"}]},{"text":" metadata for every flag, enforced by a single unit test rather than the wire format (the JSON stays dumb and fail-open). Declare a manifest with the type-erasing factories — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"owner"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expires"},{"text":" are non-optional, so a flag can’t be registered without them — and the keys are single-sourced from the typed flag declarations:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["enum FlagManifest {","    static let all: [FlagDescriptor] = [","        .bool(.newOnboarding, owner: \"growth\",","              expires: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1_788_000_000), purpose: \"New onboarding flow\"),","        .variant(.checkoutLayout, owner: \"checkout\",","                 expires: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1_785_000_000), purpose: \"Checkout A\/B\"),","    ]","}","","@Test func noForeverFlags() {","    let report = FlagGovernance.expirationReport(FlagManifest.all)","    #expect(report == nil, \"\\(report ?? \"\")\")   \/\/ failure names each expired flag + owner","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When a flag passes its expiry, the test fails and the report names the flag, its owner, and how long it’s been expired — so a stale flag gets retired instead of living forever. This has no effect on runtime evaluation.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The manifest is the single declaration site, so a typed flag key never added to it escapes governance. Closing that gap fully would need a macro; until then, convention plus code review covers it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"anchor":"Exposure-tracking","text":"Exposure tracking","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A\/B testing is only analytically valid if you know which users actually saw each variant — bucketing alone is insufficient because the code path branching on the flag might never execute."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["store.send(.featureFlags(.recordExposure(key: \"checkout_layout\")))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or via the SwiftUI sugar:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["WizardView()","    .recordsExposure(of: .checkoutLayout, store: store, action: AppAction.featureFlags)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin dedupes per session and fires the optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"onExposure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" callback (passed at plugin init). Wire that callback to your analytics plugin to forward exposures as events.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Refresh policy","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Refresh-policy"},{"code":["public enum RefreshPolicy: Sendable {","    case manual                                      \/\/ every .refresh fetches","    case automatic(minInterval: TimeInterval)        \/\/ debounce; default 300s","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Apps dispatch ","type":"text"},{"code":".refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"App.scenePhase"},{"text":" transitions; the plugin’s debouncing makes this safe to call frequently. The plugin does not subscribe to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIApplication"},{"text":" notifications — wiring stays in the host app.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Service protocol","anchor":"Service-protocol","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol FeatureFlagsService: Sendable {","    func fetch() async throws -> FeatureFlagsConfig","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One method. Caching, hydration, evaluation all live in the plugin."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Built-in: `HTTPFeatureFlagsService`","anchor":"Built-in-HTTPFeatureFlagsService","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"code":"JSONDecoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Apps host their JSON anywhere — static file on a CDN, Cloudflare Worker, their own server. Zero backend infrastructure required. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Examples\/ConfigWorker\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a runnable shared Worker serving flags + killswitch for a whole portfolio from one URL (","type":"text"},{"code":"GET \/<appID>\/flags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The URL must be "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"HTTPS"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"type":"text","text":" is allowed only for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localhost"},{"type":"text","text":" development servers; anything else is a precondition failure at init). Responses over 1 MB and non-2xx statuses throw, and malformed variant definitions (empty array, negative weights, weights not summing to 100) fail decoding — in every case the plugin keeps its last-known-good cached config."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Third-party adapters (LaunchDarkly, GrowthBook, Statsig) conform to the same protocol without changing the plugin."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Typed flag keys","level":2,"anchor":"Typed-flag-keys"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public struct BoolFlag: Sendable, Hashable","public struct VariantFlag<Variant: RawRepresentable & Sendable> where Variant.RawValue == String","public struct ValueFlag<Value: Sendable>"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read API on ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["state.isEnabled(.newOnboarding, default: false)","state.variant(of: .checkoutLayout)","state.value(of: .maxFreeUploads)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reads are pure synchronous functions. Per-property observation works as it does for any other state slice — views re-render only when the flag they read changes."}]},{"anchor":"Action-semantics-selected","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Action semantics (selected)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded(FeatureFlagsConfig, fetchedAt:)"},{"text":" is dispatched on every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refresh"},{"text":" (including debounced refreshes that return an unchanged config). Consume config transitions by observing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsState"},{"text":" or a value derived from it — not by mapping this action. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture#Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"S